 "rulebook": "No federation rule book: the roller balance board (Indo Board style rocker-roller trainer): a rigid deck 0.76 m x 0.38 m lying loose on a free roller of 0.085 m radius, with a stop under each end of the deck; the standard is the balance trainer's: time on the board with neither end of the deck nor the rider touching the floor",
 "deviations": [
  "the board: deck and roller are rigid bodies (a 2.7 kg box and a 1.8 kg hollow cylinder) with a friction coefficient of 1.0 between deck, roller and floor, without grip tape or a rubber-lined roller, because the simulator has rigid bodies only",
  "the mount: the robot starts standing on the level deck, centred over the roller (an unstable equilibrium), instead of stepping onto a deck that rests on one end, because the task is the ride, a single action"
 ],
 "texts": {
  "sentence": "Stay balanced on the roller board for 30.0 s: neither end of the deck nor any part of you may touch the floor.",
  "rules": "The board is a rigid deck 0.76 m long (left to right), 0.38 m wide and 0.018 m thick, 2.7 kg, lying loose on a roller: a free cylinder of 0.085 m radius, 0.46 m long, 1.8 kg, whose axis points fore-aft and which rolls on the floor to your left and right. Nothing holds the deck to the roller or the roller to the floor but contact and friction (coefficient 1.0); there is no spring. A stop 0.02 m high and 0.03 m long under each end of the deck keeps the roller from rolling out from under it. You succeed when 30.0 s have passed from the start without a failure. You fail the moment any part of the deck (an end or a stop) touches the floor, any part of you touches the floor or the roller, any part of you other than a foot touches the deck (a fall on the board), or neither of your feet has touched the deck for more than 1.0 s (you have left the board). With the roller in the middle, an end of the deck meets the floor at a tilt of about 24 degrees.",
  "venue": "You face +x, standing upright in the rest pose with your feet side by side on the middle of the deck, 0.24 m apart, one on each side of the roller, whose axis runs fore-aft under you; at t = 0 the deck is level, its top 0.188 m above the floor, with the roller under its middle and your centre of mass over the roller's line of contact. That is an equilibrium, and an unstable one: left alone, the robot's stance does not correct it and the board runs out from under you within a few seconds. The floor is all around.",
  "difficulty": "Two unstable motions are coupled: the deck tilts on the roller and the roller rolls away under the deck. Neither the platform's stance nor the walking policy corrects them; the legs have to shift the body's weight against the board fast enough to keep the roller between the feet for 30.0 s."
 },
